{"created": "2026-06-17T21:40:04.635373+00:00", "modified": "2026-06-17T21:40:05.262382+00:00", "id": 20736551, "conceptrecid": "18554918", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20736551", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.18554918", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20736551", "metadata": {"title": "PteroSet", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20736551", "publication_date": "2026-06-17", "description": "<div>\n<p>This release provides a curated passive acoustic monitoring dataset of Neotropical bird vocalizations recorded in Colombia (Puerto As&iacute;s, Putumayo; Pijavay, Magdalena) between 2023 and 2025.</p>\n<p>Audio was collected using autonomous AudioMoth recorders and stored in WAV format, distributed across the five project folders (MAP1, PPA1, PPA2, PPA3, PPA4). The collection comprises 563 recordings totaling 73.62 hours at a 192 kHz sample rate. The dataset contains 15,372 curated bird-event annotations at the taxonomic-group level, of which 6,702 include species-level determinations using standardized species codes in the species.csv lookup table.</p>\n<p>Each recording is paired with expert-generated annotations created in Raven Pro (labels.zip) and subsequently harmonized into a COCO-inspired JSON schema for bioacoustics. These annotations are provided in two versions: annotations_identification.json, containing all annotations, and annotations_species.json, containing only species-level annotations. Annotations are provided as strong labels with explicit temporal boundaries (t_min, t_max) and spectral bounds (f_min, f_max), enabling time-frequency localization and event detection tasks.</p>\n<p>Deployment details are distributed in metadata.csv. Additionally, model weights are included in checkpoints.zip, enabling benchmarking of bioacoustic models on this dataset.</p>\n<p>All code used for data processing and technical validation is available at&nbsp; <a href=\"https://github.com/microsoft/PteroSet\">microsoft/PteroSet</a> to ensure reproducibility. A detailed description of the methodology is provided in the accompanying <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.20578\">preprint</a>. Additional non-annotated recordings from these deployments are available upon request.</p>\n</div>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Ruiz, Daniela", "affiliation": "Microsoft AI for Good", "orcid": "0000-0001-6636-1173"}, {"name": "Ulloa, Juan Sebastian", "affiliation": "Alexander von Humboldt Biological Resources Research Institute", "orcid": "0000-0001-5666-6942"}, {"name": "Miao, Zhongqi", "affiliation": "Microsoft AI for Good", "orcid": "0000-0002-0439-8592"}, {"name": "Betancourt, Nicol\u00e1s", "affiliation": "Alexander von Humboldt Biological Resources Research Institute"}, {"name": "Hern\u00e1ndez, Andr\u00e9s", "affiliation": "Microsoft AI for Good", "orcid": "0009-0001-2589-8473"}, {"name": "Demuro, Bruno", "affiliation": "Microsoft AI for Good", "orcid": "0000-0001-9922-8811"}, {"name": "Barona Cort\u00e9s, Eliana", "affiliation": "Alexander von Humboldt Biological Resources Research Institute", "orcid": "0000-0002-9451-7996"}, {"name": "Toro G\u00f3mez, Maria Paula", "affiliation": "Alexander von Humboldt Biological Resources Research Institute", "orcid": "0000-0001-8875-6619"}, {"name": "Mendoza-Henao, Angela M.", "affiliation": "Alexander von Humboldt Biological Resources Research Institute", "orcid": "0000-0002-6752-9238"}, {"name": "Sierra-Ricaurte, Andres Felipe", "affiliation": "Alexander von Humboldt Biological Resources Research Institute", "orcid": "0000-0002-7168-373X"}, {"name": "P\u00e9rez-Pe\u00f1a, Sebastian Camilo", "affiliation": "Louisiana State University", "orcid": "0000-0003-2501-2334"}, {"name": "Dodhia, Rahul", "affiliation": "Microsoft AI for Good", "orcid": "0000-0003-3812-3906"}, {"name": "Arbelaez, Pablo", "affiliation": "Universidad de Los Andes", "orcid": "0000-0001-5244-2407"}, {"name": "Lavista Ferres, Juan M.", "affiliation": "Microsoft AI for Good", "orcid": "0000-0002-9654-3178"}], "resource_type"